      "math_academy_id": "q-40305",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le z\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[y]_{y=1}^{y={x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2)-1\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[({x}^{2}+1)z+\\frac{2{z}^{3}}{3}]}_{z=-1}^{z=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+1)(1-(-1))+\\frac{2}{3}({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}+\\frac{10}{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{10}{3}x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{3}(2)^{3}+\\frac{10}{3}(2))-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
      "grade": "Correct",
